:HELP NAME=ADDLNK.Add Link (ADDLNK)
:P.The Add Link (ADDLNK) command works with a symbolic or hard link to
an object.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLNK/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLNK/NEWLNK'.New link (NEWLNK)
:P.The new link for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLNK/LNKTYPE'.Link type (LNKTYPE)
:P.The link type for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYMBOLIC, *HARD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDMFS.Add Mounted FS (ADDMFS)
:P.Use the Add Mounted File System (ADDMFS) command to mount a file
system over a directory&colon. a remote NFS export, or a user-defined
file system. It is MOUNT under another name. You need *IOSYSCFG special
authority.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/TYPE'.Type of file system (TYPE)
:P.The kind of file system&colon. *NFS an export of another system,
*UDFS a user-defined file system of this one.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NFS, *UDFS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/MFS'.File system to mount (MFS)
:P.The file system to mount&colon. for *NFS host&colon.path, for *UDFS
the path of the user-defined file system.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/MNTOVRDIR'.Directory to mount over (MNTOVRDIR)
:P.The directory the file system is mounted over.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/OPTIONS'.Mount options (OPTIONS)
:P.Mount options, separated by commas, as MOUNT's help lists them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 250 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *DFT is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.For *NFS&colon. the CCSIDs the remote files' data and path names are
in. Not with CODEPAGE.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Data file CCSID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BINARY:EPK.
:PD.Binary&colon. no conversion.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Path name CCSID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/CODEPAGE'.Code page (CODEPAGE)
:P.For *NFS&colon. the code pages of the remote files' data and path
names. Not with CCSID.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Data file code page
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BINARY:EPK.
:PD.Binary&colon. no conversion.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Path name code page
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CD.Change Current Directory (CD)
:P.Use the Change Current Directory (CD) command to change the job's
current directory (CHGCURDIR's alias).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CD/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGATR.Change Attribute (CHGATR)
:P.Use the Change Attribute (CHGATR) command to change one attribute of
IFS objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/ATR'.Attribute (ATR)
:P.The attribute for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID determines the conversion.
:PT.:PK.*TEXT:EPK.
:PD.Text.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *READONLY, *HIDDEN, *PCSYSTEM, *PCARCHIVE,
*SYSARCHIVE, *ALWCKPWRT, *USECOUNT, *DISKSTGOPT, *MAINSTGOPT,
*CRTOBJSCAN, *SCAN, *ALWSAV, *RSTDRNMUNL, *SETUID, *SETGID, *CRTOBJAUD,
*INHCKPWRT, *RUNEXIT, *CRTRUNEXIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/VALUE'.New value (VALUE)
:P.The new value for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:PT.:PK.*CHGONLY:EPK.
:PD.Changes only.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RESET, *MINIMIZE, *DYNAMIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/SYMLNK'.Symbolic link (SYMLNK)
:P.Whether to symbolic link.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/TEXT'.Text description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGCURDIR.Change Current Directory (CHGCURDIR)
:P.Use the Change Current Directory (CHGCURDIR) command to change the
job's current directory.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCURDIR/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGNFSEXP.Change NFS Export (CHGNFSEXP)
:P.Use the Change NFS Export (CHGNFSEXP) command to make directories
available to NFS clients, to change how they are exported, or to end
their export. It is EXPORTFS under another name. You need *IOSYSCFG
special authority.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGNFSEXP/OPTIONS'.NFS export options (OPTIONS)
:P.The flags and export options, as EXPORTFS's help lists them. *DFT
exports DIR with the options /etc/exports gives it, or the defaults when
it has no entry.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 200 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *DFT is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGNFSEXP/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory to export or whose export ends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGNFSEXP/HOSTOPT'.Host options (HOSTOPT)
:P.Options for some clients of the export&colon. the host, the CCSID
file data is converted to for it, the CCSID of its path names, and
whether its writes are written to disk before the answer.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.No host options&colon. file data is not converted, path names are
ASCII and writes are synchronous.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Host name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Data file CCSID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BINARY:EPK.
:PD.Binary&colon. no conversion.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Path name CCSID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Force synchronous write
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYNC, *ASYNC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHKIN.Check In Object (CHKIN)
:P.Use the Check In Object (CHKIN) command to check an IFS object back
in.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKIN/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKIN/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHKOUT.Check Out Object (CHKOUT)
:P.Use the Check Out Object (CHKOUT) command to check an IFS object out;
others may read it only.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKOUT/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKOUT/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPY.Copy Object (CPY)
:P.Use the Copy Object (CPY) command to copy objects, a directory's
contents with SUBTREE(*ALL).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/TODIR'.To directory (TODIR)
:P.The to directory for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '.' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/TOOBJ'.To object (TOOBJ)
:P.The to object for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/SYMLNK'.Symbolic link (SYMLNK)
:P.Whether to symbolic link.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/FROMCCSID'.From CCSID (FROMCCSID)
:P.The CCSID the data is in.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/TOCCSID'.To CCSID (TOCCSID)
:P.The to CCSID for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/DTAFMT'.Data format (DTAFMT)
:P.The format of the data&colon. fixed-length fields or delimited.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BINARY:EPK.
:PD.Binary&colon. no conversion.
:PT.:PK.*TEXT:EPK.
:PD.Text.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NODIR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/REPLACE'.Replace object (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/OWNER'.Owner (OWNER)
:P.The owner of the objects created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ, *INDIROBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/FROMCODPAG'.From code page (FROMCODPAG)
:P.The from code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/TOCODEPAGE'.To code page (TOCODEPAGE)
:P.The to code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYFRMSTMF.Copy From Stream File (CPYFRMSTMF)
:P.Use the Copy From Stream File (CPYFRMSTMF) command to copy a stream
file's lines into a database member.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/FROMSTMF'.Stream file to read (FROMSTMF)
:P.The stream file to read for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/TOMBR'.Member path to write (TOMBR)
:P.The member of the to-file that receives the data.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/MBROPT'.When the member exists (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/CVTDTA'.Data conversion (CVTDTA)
:P.The data conversion for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TBL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/STMFCCSID'.Stream file data CCSID (STMFCCSID)
:P.The stream file data CCSID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMF:EPK.
:PD.A stream file.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/DBFCCSID'.Member data CCSID (DBFCCSID)
:P.The member data CCSID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/TBL'.Conversion table path (TBL)
:P.The conversion table path for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/ENDLINFMT'.Line ends read (ENDLINFMT)
:P.The line ends read for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CRLF:EPK.
:PD.Carriage return and line feed.
:PT.:PK.*LF:EPK.
:PD.Line feed.
:PT.:PK.*CR:EPK.
:PD.Carriage return.
:PT.:PK.*FIXED:EPK.
:PD.Fixed length.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LFCR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/TABEXPN'.Tabs to blanks (TABEXPN)
:P.Whether to tabs to blanks.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/STMFCODPAG'.Stream file code page (STMFCODPAG)
:P.The stream file code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMF:EPK.
:PD.A stream file.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYTOSTMF.Copy To Stream File (CPYTOSTMF)
:P.Use the Copy To Stream File (CPYTOSTMF) command to copy a database
member's records into a stream file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/FROMMBR'.Member path to copy (FROMMBR)
:P.The member the data comes from.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/TOSTMF'.Stream file to write (TOSTMF)
:P.The stream file to write for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/STMFOPT'.When the stream file exists (STMFOPT)
:P.The when the stream file exists for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/CVTDTA'.Data conversion (CVTDTA)
:P.The data conversion for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TBL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/DBFCCSID'.Member data CCSID (DBFCCSID)
:P.The member data CCSID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/STMFCCSID'.Stream file data CCSID (STMFCCSID)
:P.The stream file data CCSID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMF:EPK.
:PD.A stream file.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/TBL'.Conversion table path (TBL)
:P.The conversion table path for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/ENDLINFMT'.Line end written (ENDLINFMT)
:P.The line end written for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CRLF:EPK.
:PD.Carriage return and line feed.
:PT.:PK.*LF:EPK.
:PD.Line feed.
:PT.:PK.*CR:EPK.
:PD.Carriage return.
:PT.:PK.*FIXED:EPK.
:PD.Fixed length.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LFCR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/AUT'.Authority of a new file (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INDIRFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/STMFCODPAG'.Stream file code page (STMFCODPAG)
:P.The stream file code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMF:EPK.
:PD.A stream file.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTDIR.Create Directory (CRTDIR)
:P.Use the Create Directory (CRTDIR) command to make a directory (MD and
MKDIR are the same command).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/DTAAUT'.Public authority for data (DTAAUT)
:P.The data authorities&colon. read, add, update, delete and execute.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RWX, *RW, *RX, *WX, *R, *W, *X.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/OBJAUT'.Public authority for object (OBJAUT)
:P.The object authorities&colon. operational, management, existence,
alter and reference.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/CRTOBJAUD'.Auditing value for objects (CRTOBJAUD)
:P.The auditing value given to objects created in the library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/CRTOBJSCAN'.Scanning option for objects (CRTOBJSCAN)
:P.Whether objects created in the library are scanned by the exit
programs of the scan exit points.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*CHGONLY:EPK.
:PD.Changes only.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PARENT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/RSTDRNMUNL'.Restricted rename and unlink (RSTDRNMUNL)
:P.Whether renaming and unlinking objects in the directory is restricted
to their owners.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTUDFS.Create User-Defined FS (CRTUDFS)
:P.Use the Create User-Defined FS (CRTUDFS) command to make a
user-defined file system, /dev/QASPnn/NAME.udfs.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTUDFS/UDFS'.User-defined file system (UDFS)
:P.The user-defined file system for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTUDFS/DTAAUT'.Public authority for data (DTAAUT)
:P.The data authorities&colon. read, add, update, delete and execute.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RWX, *RW, *RX, *WX, *R, *W, *X.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTUDFS/OBJAUT'.Public authority for object (OBJAUT)
:P.The object authorities&colon. operational, management, existence,
alter and reference.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTUDFS/CRTOBJAUD'.Auditing value for objects (CRTOBJAUD)
:P.The auditing value given to objects created in the library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTUDFS/CRTOBJSCAN'.Scanning option for objects (CRTOBJSCAN)
:P.Whether objects created in the library are scanned by the exit
programs of the scan exit points.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*CHGONLY:EPK.
:PD.Changes only.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PARENT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTUDFS/RSTDRNMUNL'.Restricted rename and unlink (RSTDRNMUNL)
:P.Whether renaming and unlinking objects in the directory is restricted
to their owners.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTUDFS/CASE'.Case sensitivity (CASE)
:P.The case sensitivity for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MONO, *MIXED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTUDFS/DFTFILEFMT'.Default file format (DFTFILEFMT)
:P.The default file format for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TYPE2:EPK.
:PD.Type 2.
:PT.:PK.*TYPE1:EPK.
:PD.Type 1.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTUDFS/TEXT'.Text description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DEL.Remove Link (DEL)
:P.Use the Remove Link (DEL) command to remove a link (RMVLNK's alias).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DEL/OBJLNK'.Object link (OBJLNK)
:P.The object link for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTUDFS.Delete User-Defined FS (DLTUDFS)
:P.Use the Delete User-Defined FS (DLTUDFS) command to delete a
user-defined file system that is not mounted.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTUDFS/UDFS'.User-defined file system (UDFS)
:P.The user-defined file system for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPLNK.Display Object Links (DSPLNK)
:P.The Display Object Links (DSPLNK) command works with the links a path
names.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLNK/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLNK/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLNK/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:PARML.
