:HELP NAME='DSPLNK/DETAIL'.Detail (DETAIL)
:P.The detail for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*NAME:EPK.
:PD.By name.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*EXTENDED:EPK.
:PD.Extended detail.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLNK/DSPOPT'.Display option (DSPOPT)
:P.The display option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPMFSINF.Display Mounted FS Information (DSPMFSINF)
:P.Use the Display Mounted File System Information (DSPMFSINF) command
to show the attributes of the file system an object is in&colon. its
type, its size and free space, its limits, and how it is mounted.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMFSINF/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.A path name of any object in the file system.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMFSINF/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Whether the information is shown or printed to a spooled file of
QPRINT.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The information is shown at a display; a batch job prints it.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPUDFS.Display User-Defined FS (DSPUDFS)
:P.The Display User-Defined FS (DSPUDFS) command works with a
user-defined file system's attributes and mounts.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPUDFS/UDFS'.User-defined file system (UDFS)
:P.The user-defined file system for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPUDFS/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDNFSSVR.End NFS Server (ENDNFSSVR)
:P.Use the End NFS Server (ENDNFSSVR) command to end the Network File
System server daemons&colon. one type, or every type in the reverse of
the order they start in. You need *IOSYSCFG special authority.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDNFSSVR/SERVER'.Server daemon (SERVER)
:P.The type of daemon to end, or *ALL for every type running. *GSS is
refused&colon. Kerberos is not supported.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.Every daemon type running, ended in the order *NLM, *NSM, *MNT,
*SVR, *RGY, *BIO, *RPC.
:PT.:PK.*GSS:EPK.
:PD.The Kerberos daemon, which this system does not have&colon. the
command fails.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RPC, *BIO, *RGY, *SVR, *MNT, *NSM, *NLM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDNFSSVR/ENDJOBTIMO'.Timeout for end of daemon (ENDJOBTIMO)
:P.How many seconds to wait for each daemon to end, from 1 to 3600. When
the time passes the command stops with a message saying the daemon may
still be running.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.Wait as long as it takes.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 3600.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 30 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDRPCBIND.End RPC Binder Daemon (ENDRPCBIND)
:P.Use the End RPC Binder Daemon (ENDRPCBIND) command to end the binder.
Its registrations are saved in /etc/RPCBTAB for the next start. You need
*IOSYSCFG special authority.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=EXPORTFS.Change NFS Export (EXPORTFS)
:P.Use the Change NFS Export (EXPORTFS) command to make directories
available to NFS clients, to change how they are exported, or to end
their export. The export table lasts until the next IPL; entries kept in
/etc/exports are exported again with OPTIONS('-A'). You need *IOSYSCFG
special authority.
:P.The flags of OPTIONS&colon. -A every entry of /etc/exports; -I DIR
without reading /etc/exports; -U end the export of DIR, or with -A of
every entry; -F with -U, end it whatever the clients hold; -O followed
by the export options; -E an escape message when an entry fails; -V a
message for each entry. Export options&colon. RO, RW=host&colon.host,
ACCESS=host&colon.host, ROOT=host&colon.host, ANON=uid, NOSUID, SEC=sys,
VERS=3&colon.4, PUBLIC, NFSROOT=path, EXNAME=path. A host is a name, an
address, @network/length or a netgroup of /etc/netgroup.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='EXPORTFS/OPTIONS'.NFS export options (OPTIONS)
:P.The flags and export options, as the command's help lists them. *DFT
exports DIR with the options /etc/exports gives it, or the defaults when
it has no entry.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 200 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *DFT is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='EXPORTFS/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory to export or whose export ends. Directories in /QOPT,
/QDLS, /QNTC, /QFileSvr.400 and in an NFS mount cannot be exported.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='EXPORTFS/HOSTOPT'.Host options (HOSTOPT)
:P.Options for some clients of the export&colon. the host, the CCSID
file data is converted to for it, the CCSID of its path names, and
whether its writes are written to disk before the answer.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.No host options&colon. file data is not converted, path names are
ASCII and writes are synchronous.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Host name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Data file CCSID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BINARY:EPK.
:PD.Binary&colon. no conversion.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Path name CCSID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Force synchronous write
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYNC, *ASYNC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=MD.Create Directory (MD)
:P.Use the Create Directory (MD) command to make a directory (CRTDIR's
alias).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MD/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MD/DTAAUT'.Public authority for data (DTAAUT)
:P.The data authorities&colon. read, add, update, delete and execute.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RWX, *RW, *RX, *WX, *R, *W, *X.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MD/OBJAUT'.Public authority for object (OBJAUT)
:P.The object authorities&colon. operational, management, existence,
alter and reference.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MD/CRTOBJAUD'.Auditing value for objects (CRTOBJAUD)
:P.The auditing value given to objects created in the library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MD/CRTOBJSCAN'.Scanning option for objects (CRTOBJSCAN)
:P.Whether objects created in the library are scanned by the exit
programs of the scan exit points.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*CHGONLY:EPK.
:PD.Changes only.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PARENT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MD/RSTDRNMUNL'.Restricted rename and unlink (RSTDRNMUNL)
:P.Whether renaming and unlinking objects in the directory is restricted
to their owners.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=MKDIR.Create Directory (MKDIR)
:P.Use the Create Directory (MKDIR) command to make a directory
(CRTDIR's alias).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MKDIR/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MKDIR/DTAAUT'.Public authority for data (DTAAUT)
:P.The data authorities&colon. read, add, update, delete and execute.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RWX, *RW, *RX, *WX, *R, *W, *X.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MKDIR/OBJAUT'.Public authority for object (OBJAUT)
:P.The object authorities&colon. operational, management, existence,
alter and reference.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MKDIR/CRTOBJAUD'.Auditing value for objects (CRTOBJAUD)
:P.The auditing value given to objects created in the library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MKDIR/CRTOBJSCAN'.Scanning option for objects (CRTOBJSCAN)
:P.Whether objects created in the library are scanned by the exit
programs of the scan exit points.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*CHGONLY:EPK.
:PD.Changes only.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PARENT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MKDIR/RSTDRNMUNL'.Restricted rename and unlink (RSTDRNMUNL)
:P.Whether renaming and unlinking objects in the directory is restricted
to their owners.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=MOUNT.Add Mounted FS (MOUNT)
:P.Use the Add Mounted File System (MOUNT) command to mount a file
system over a directory&colon. a remote NFS export, or a user-defined
file system. The directory shows the file system's contents until it is
unmounted or the next IPL. You need *IOSYSCFG special authority.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/TYPE'.Type of file system (TYPE)
:P.The kind of file system&colon. *NFS an export of another system,
*UDFS a user-defined file system of this one.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NFS:EPK.
:PD.An export of an NFS server, named host&colon.path in MFS.
:PT.:PK.*UDFS:EPK.
:PD.A user-defined file system, named /dev/QASPnn/name.udfs in MFS.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/MFS'.File system to mount (MFS)
:P.The file system to mount&colon. for *NFS the server's name or
address, a colon and the path of the export; for *UDFS the path of the
user-defined file system.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/MNTOVRDIR'.Directory to mount over (MNTOVRDIR)
:P.The directory the file system is mounted over. It must exist; what it
holds is hidden while the mount lasts.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/OPTIONS'.Mount options (OPTIONS)
:P.Mount options, separated by commas&colon. rw or ro, suid or nosuid,
soft or hard, intr or nointr, retry=, rsize=, wsize=, timeo=, retrans=,
acregmin=, acregmax=, acdirmin=, acdirmax=, actimeo=, noac, vers=,
proto=, port=, mountport=, sec=sys. For *UDFS only rw and ro apply.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 250 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *DFT is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.For *NFS&colon. the CCSIDs the remote files' data and path names are
in, so that they are converted. Not with CODEPAGE.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Data file CCSID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BINARY:EPK.
:PD.Binary&colon. no conversion.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Path name CCSID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/CODEPAGE'.Code page (CODEPAGE)
:P.For *NFS&colon. the code pages the remote files' data and path names
are in, given as code pages instead of CCSIDs. Not with CCSID.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Data file code page
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BINARY:EPK.
:PD.Binary&colon. no conversion.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Path name code page
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=MOV.Move Object (MOV)
:P.Use the Move Object (MOV) command to move objects to another
directory or name.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/TODIR'.To directory (TODIR)
:P.The to directory for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '.' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/TOOBJ'.To object (TOOBJ)
:P.The to object for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/FROMCCSID'.From CCSID (FROMCCSID)
:P.The CCSID the data is in.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/TOCCSID'.To CCSID (TOCCSID)
:P.The to CCSID for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/DTAFMT'.Data format (DTAFMT)
:P.The format of the data&colon. fixed-length fields or delimited.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BINARY:EPK.
:PD.Binary&colon. no conversion.
:PT.:PK.*TEXT:EPK.
:PD.Text.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/FROMCODPAG'.From code page (FROMCODPAG)
:P.The from code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/TOCODEPAGE'.To code page (TOCODEPAGE)
:P.The to code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RCLLNK.Reclaim Object Links (RCLLNK)
:P.Use the Reclaim Object Links (RCLLNK) command to reclaim the
IFS&colon. attributes, owners, authorities, links.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLLNK/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLLNK/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DIR:EPK.
:PD.The directory and the objects in it, but not its subdirectories'
contents.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLLNK/DMGOBJOPT'.Damaged object option (DMGOBJOPT)
:P.The damaged object option for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object option
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PK.*DELETE:EPK.
:PD.Deleted.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Unusable directory option
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DELETE:EPK.
:PD.Deleted.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RD.Remove Directory (RD)
:P.Use the Remove Directory (RD) command to remove a directory (RMDIR's
alias).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RD/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RD/SUBTREE'.Remove subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RD/RMVLNK'.Remove links in directory (RMVLNK)
:P.Whether to remove links in directory.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=REN.Rename Object (REN)
:P.Use the Rename Object (REN) command to rename an object link (RNM's
alias).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='REN/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='REN/NEWOBJ'.New object name (NEWOBJ)
:P.The new object name for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RLSIFSLCK.Release File System Locks (RLSIFSLCK)
:P.Use the Release File System Locks (RLSIFSLCK) command to release
byte-range locks that are no longer wanted&colon. those an NFS client
holds through this system's server, or those held on an object or on its
whole file system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RLSIFSLCK/RMTLOCNAME'.Remote location (RMTLOCNAME)
:P.The host name or address of an NFS client whose locks the *NLM daemon
releases. Not with OBJ.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RLSIFSLCK/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object whose byte-range locks are released. Not with RMTLOCNAME.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RLSIFSLCK/NFSSVRLCK'.NFS Server locks (NFSSVRLCK)
:P.Whether the locks NFS clients hold on the object through the *NLM
daemon are released.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RLSIFSLCK/LCLBRNGLCK'.Local byte-range locks (LCLBRNGLCK)
:P.Whether the byte-range locks local jobs hold on the object are
released. Not *YES with OBJMFS(*YES).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RLSIFSLCK/OBJMFS'.Object's file system (OBJMFS)
:P.Whether the byte-range locks local jobs hold on every object of the
object's file system are released. Not *YES with LCLBRNGLCK(*YES).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMDIR.Remove Directory (RMDIR)
:P.Use the Remove Directory (RMDIR) command to remove a directory (RD is
the same command).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMDIR/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMDIR/SUBTREE'.Remove subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMDIR/RMVLNK'.Remove links in directory (RMVLNK)
:P.Whether to remove links in directory.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVLNK.Remove Link (RMVLNK)
:P.Use the Remove Link (RMVLNK) command to remove a link; a pattern in
the last name removes each match.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVLNK/OBJLNK'.Object link (OBJLNK)
:P.The object link for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVMFS.Remove Mounted FS (RMVMFS)
:P.Use the Remove Mounted File System (RMVMFS) command to unmount a file
system from the directory it is mounted over. It is UNMOUNT under
another name. You need *IOSYSCFG special authority.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMFS/TYPE'.Type of file system (TYPE)
:P.The kind of file system to unmount&colon. *NFS, *UDFS, or *ALL for
whatever is mounted there.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NFS, *UDFS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMFS/MNTOVRDIR'.Directory mounted over (MNTOVRDIR)
:P.The directory the file system is mounted over. *ALL unmounts every
mounted file system and needs TYPE(*ALL).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.Every mounted file system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMFS/MFS'.Mounted file system (MFS)
:P.For *UDFS&colon. the user-defined file system to unmount, instead of
the directory.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RNM.Rename Object (RNM)
:P.Use the Rename Object (RNM) command to give an object link a new name
in its directory.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RNM/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RNM/NEWOBJ'.New object name (NEWOBJ)
:P.The new object name for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RPCBIND.Start RPC Binder Daemon (RPCBIND)
:P.Use the Start RPC Binder Daemon (RPCBIND) command to start the binder
alone&colon. the daemon that tells RPC clients on which ports this
system's RPC programs listen (port 111). You need *IOSYSCFG special
authority.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RPCBIND/RTVRPCREG'.Retrieve RPC registration (RTVRPCREG)
:P.Whether the binder starts with the registrations it saved in
/etc/RPCBTAB when it last ended.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The binder starts with no registrations.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The saved registrations are read back.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTVCURDIR.Retrieve Current Directory (RTVCURDIR)
:P.The Retrieve Current Directory (RTVCURDIR) command works with the
job's current directory into CL variables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCURDIR/RTNDIR'.CL var for current directory (RTNDIR)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of current directory. Give a
character variable of at least 5000 characters.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCURDIR/DIRNAMLEN'.CL var for directory length (DIRNAMLEN)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of directory length. Give a
decimal variable of 7 digits, 0 after the point.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STATFS.Display Mounted FS Information (STATFS)
:P.Use the Display Mounted File System Information (STATFS) command to
show the attributes of the file system an object is in. It is DSPMFSINF
under another name.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STATFS/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.A path name of any object in the file system.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STATFS/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Whether the information is shown or printed to a spooled file of
QPRINT.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The information is shown at a display; a batch job prints it.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRNFSSVR.Start NFS Server (STRNFSSVR)
:P.Use the Start NFS Server (STRNFSSVR) command to start the Network
File System server daemons&colon. one type, or every type in the order
NFS needs them. Each daemon is a job in subsystem QSYSWRK; the command
waits for it to report that it is ready. You need *IOSYSCFG special
authority.
:P.The RPC binder is started first when a daemon that registers with it
is asked for and the binder is not running. A daemon already running is
left as it is and reported with a diagnostic message.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRNFSSVR/SERVER'.Server daemon (SERVER)
:P.The type of daemon to start, or *ALL for every type&colon. *RPC the
binder (port 111), *BIO the block I/O daemons of the client, *RGY the
NFSv4 identity mapping, *SVR the server (port 2049), *MNT the mount
daemon, *NSM the status monitor and *NLM the lock manager. *GSS is
refused&colon. Kerberos is not supported.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.Every daemon type, started in the order *RPC, *BIO, *RGY, *SVR,
*MNT, *NSM, *NLM.
:PT.:PK.*GSS:EPK.
:PD.The Kerberos daemon, which this system does not have&colon. the
command fails.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RPC, *BIO, *RGY, *SVR, *MNT, *NSM, *NLM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRNFSSVR/NBRSVR'.Number of server daemons (NBRSVR)
:P.How many server daemon jobs (*SVR) to start, from 1 to 20. Several
jobs share the connections of the clients. Only with SERVER(*SVR) or
SERVER(*ALL).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 20.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRNFSSVR/NBRBIO'.Number of block I/O daemons (NBRBIO)
:P.How many block I/O daemon jobs (*BIO) to start, from 1 to 20&colon.
they read ahead and write behind for this system's NFS mounts. Only with
SERVER(*BIO) or SERVER(*ALL).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 20.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRNFSSVR/RTVRPCREG'.Retrieve RPC registration (RTVRPCREG)
:P.Whether the binder starts with the registrations it saved in
/etc/RPCBTAB when it last ended. Only with SERVER(*RPC) or SERVER(*ALL).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The binder starts with no registrations.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The saved registrations are read back.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRNFSSVR/STRJOBTIMO'.Timeout for start of daemon (STRJOBTIMO)
:P.How many seconds to wait for each daemon to report that it is ready,
from 1 to 3600. When the time passes the command stops with a message
saying the daemon may not have started.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.Wait as long as it takes.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 3600.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 30 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=UNMOUNT.Remove Mounted FS (UNMOUNT)
:P.Use the Remove Mounted File System (UNMOUNT) command to unmount a
file system from the directory it is mounted over, or every mounted file
system at once. You need *IOSYSCFG special authority.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UNMOUNT/TYPE'.Type of file system (TYPE)
:P.The kind of file system to unmount&colon. *NFS, *UDFS, or *ALL for
whatever is mounted there.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.Every file system mounted over the directory, or with
MNTOVRDIR(*ALL) every mounted file system.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NFS, *UDFS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UNMOUNT/MNTOVRDIR'.Directory mounted over (MNTOVRDIR)
:P.The directory the file system is mounted over. *ALL unmounts every
mounted file system and needs TYPE(*ALL).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.Every mounted file system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UNMOUNT/MFS'.Mounted file system (MFS)
:P.For *UDFS&colon. the user-defined file system to unmount, instead of
the directory.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKLNK.Work with Object Links (WRKLNK)
:P.The Work with Object Links (WRKLNK) command works with the links a
path names, with options to work on them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLNK/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLNK/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
